<!--Post: 54--><!--Time: 1085299144-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST54"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ohenry<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ohenry<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, May 23, 2004 - 12:59 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I am hoping for confirmation of a &#39;rumor&#39;&#40;?&#41; floating around other message boards. There are some claiming that this Tuesday, May 25, KAKE news &#40;ABC affiliate, ch. 10 in Wichita market&#41; will air an exclusive interview with known BTK survivor Kevin Bright &#40;Kathryn&#39;s brother&#41;. Has anyone else heard this? I am so hoping that it is true, for it would almost certainly be very enlightening. I would much appreciate any information that anybody might have in regards to this. Thank you in advance.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 54-->
<!--Post: 61--><!--Time: 1085352599-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST61"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Doone<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Doone<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, May 23, 2004 - 3:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes KAKE will air an interview with Kevin tuesday on the 10 pm news.  Hope it is enlightening.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 61-->
<!--Post: 70--><!--Time: 1085377956-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST70"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ohenry<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ohenry<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, May 23, 2004 - 10:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Fantastic! Thank you for the reply. I am sure Mr. Bright relives parts of that horrible day EVERY day. Not only was he nearly murdered, but the fact that he had to listen to his sister dying was probably harder for him. As much as we want BTK apprehended, imagine what it would mean to Kevin. He would rest peacefully, I would think, for maybe the first time in 27 years. As the only adult who knowingly came into personal face-to-face contact with BTK, his memory of that day could be crucial to the case. Can&#39;t wait to see the interview. <BR> <BR>Thanx again, Doone.  -O&#39;Henry<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 70-->
<!--Post: 80--><!--Time: 1085510184-->
