</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, May 25, 2004 - 12:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok, I must have only glimpsed a recent newspaper article about Kevin.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 83-->
<!--Post: 85--><!--Time: 1085538119-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST85"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Caligirl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Caligirl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, May 25, 2004 - 7:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Is it only going to be broadcast in the Witchita area?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 85-->
<!--Post: 87--><!--Time: 1085538602-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST87"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilahsue<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilahsue<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, May 25, 2004 - 7:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think so Caligirl but I&#39;m not sure.  I know that they said they would only interview Kevin Bright if he came from OK to Wichita to talk to them.  There was a big article about it somewhere on the kanas board and the EZ board.  Anyway, I do think it&#39;s only going to be broadcast locally.  It&#39;s coming on in just a half hour and I&#39;m sure I&#39;ll watch it.  I&#39;ll do my best to give the best details I can.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 87-->
<!--Post: 96--><!--Time: 1085543955-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST96"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilahsue<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilahsue<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, May 25, 2004 - 8:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.kake.com/home/headlines/794962.html" target=_top>www.kake.com/home/headlines/794962.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 96-->
<!--Post: 136--><!--Time: 1085882193-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST136"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, May 29, 2004 - 6:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Kevin got the gun away from BTK and squeezed the trigger twice? No wonder BTK took a break for a few years...talk about a close call.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 136-->
<!--Post: 156--><!--Time: 1086101041-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST156"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Warren_b<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Warren_b<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, June 01, 2004 - 7:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wonder why the gun didn&#39;t fire when Kevin pulled the trigger?  It could have been a .22 single action, where he would have had to pull the hammer back before firing.  If he didn&#39;t know that, pulling on the trigger won&#39;t do anything.  Or an automatic, where the slide would have to be retracted to chamber a round. If it was a double action, he may have confused the long and heavy trigger pull with pulling the trigger twice. Or BTK planned that if someone took the gun in a struggle, the rotation on the cylinder was set to hit an empty chamber first.  In any event, its unusual for a gun, even a cheap Saturday Nite Special, to misfire twice, and then fire.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 156-->
<!--Post: 162--><!--Time: 1086256798-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST162"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Unsub<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Unsub<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, June 03, 2004 - 2:59 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I am no expert on guns but I was wndering the same thing about the gun, how it could misfire twice. I believe it has been stated it is a revolver, the WPD from the bullets recovered even know what make/model, although I am sure that info isnt around. Not familiar with the single action so I dont know what happens when you pull the trigger, for me when I hear misfire I think, trigger pulled hammer fell.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 162-->
<!--Post: 261--><!--Time: 1086970562-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST261"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jenkins<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jenkins<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, June 11, 2004 - 9:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Seeing Kevin&#39;s description knowing he has to have the right description in mind as he was an adult is a lil bit odd as its so contradictary to what everyone else has seen, BTK is generally described as 6ft or 6&#39;2&#34; blond, thin/average &#40;not lanky&#41; and white i do believe. BTK never directly took credit for Bright, I believe it was him who killed her, and maybe the blond guy people reported seeing was never BTK to begin with but its just odd that the blond guy was reported at the Oteros and after the Fox call and I believe by Vian&#39;s kids. What gives for the mismatch? Maybe BTK didn&#39;t kill Bright????  <BR> <BR>Maybe Kevin is BTK and Katherine shot him in her own defense?? I don&#39;t believe that. <BR> <BR>But, I am quite bothered by these two completely different BTK descriptions. I take Kevins words that that is what Katherines killer looked like. He knows. I doubt he will ever forget. But its just so odd to me that the description of Katherines BTK is nothing at all like Oteros BTK or Fox&#39;s BTK or Vian&#39;s BTK. <BR> <BR> <BR>What gives???/<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 261-->
<!--Post: 504--><!--Time: 1090006927-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST504"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Screamer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Screamer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, July 16, 2004 - 12:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Not sure if this should be under media or here. Feel free to move it.  <BR> <BR>Interesting, maybe this was not BTK related? <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kake.com/home/headlines/872741.html" target=_top>http://www.kake.com/home/headlines/872741.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 504-->
<!--Post: 505--><!--Time: 1090007583-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST505"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Matt<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Matt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, July 16, 2004 - 12:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->To Jenkins; where did you come up with that as the only description for BTK? There are a couple more that vary from the tall, blonde slender man you refer to.  Also, Kevin wan&#39;t an adult at the time, he ws 17 or 18.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 505-->
<!--Post: 506--><!--Time: 1090007861-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST506"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Laoise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Laoise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, July 16, 2004 - 12:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK never actually claimed the Bright killing. As a matter of fact, after her murder and after Vian&#39;s murder, he did say in a letter that he had never left any witnesses except the Vian kids. Why would he deliberately leave out Kevin? I personally am not convinced that BTK killed Katherine Bright. I need more info about what was actually done to her first before I decide.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 506-->
<!--Post: 523--><!--Time: 1090271281-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST523"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, July 19, 2004 - 2:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Interesting point Laoise and good question! <BR>Then Bright&#39;s whole story is...I don&#39;t know...odd!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 523-->
<!--Post: 622--><!--Time: 1090960410-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST622"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 27, 2004 - 1:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It may be possible that since Kevin Bright survived, and was not a child, BTK may have felt his attack on Bright was &#34;unsuccessful,&#34; since there was a male survivor of adult age &#40;or at least adult size&#41; and the survival of Kevin may have been, to BTK, an admission of a failure, causing BTK to want to forget about the attack at the Bright residence. But I&#39;m just guessing, of course. <BR> <BR>A little similarity with Lake Berryessa and Zodiac; when he thought both victims were deceased, Zodiac seemed more boastful, painting murder dates on the male &#40;who ended up surviving&#41; <BR>victim&#39;s car and phoning the police from downtown Napa, a few blocks from the police station. <BR>When it was known that Bryan Hartnell had survived, the Zodiac suddenly went silent on the subject of the Lake Berryessa attack. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 622-->
<!--Post: 666--><!--Time: 1091377191-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST666"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, August 01, 2004 - 9:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Because of his plain vanilla appearance, BTK is hiding in plain sight.  Don&#39;t sell him short when it comes to disguises or appearance alteration.  It just occurred to me that he may be in the drama/speech field, which would account for his diction/enunciation patterns.  I took him for a pilot because I am one. However, taking these things for granted and making interpretations according to our experiences/thinking patterns is what has allowed BTK to remain at large.  What is not apparent to us may be more the important and more difficult key.   The variety of descriptions of him are so varied. Of course, eye witnesses are not always reliable because of the emotion of the moment, etc.  If BTK was wearing a black trench coat and had shaggy hair below his ears, he would have caught more attention from the fireman at the phone booth incident. As reported of many killers, they are changlings.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 666-->
<!--Post: 681--><!--Time: 1091426164-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST681"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, August 01, 2004 - 10:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->As time passes, I am becoming less and less impressed with eyewitness descriptions. Especially <BR>witness descriptions of <i>strangers</i>. I&#39;m very happy when murder cases are solved because of eyewitness information; <BR>however, police composite sketches based on witnesses have also crippled, stymied or even derailed investgative efforts, too. <BR>I guess I&#39;m saying that composite sketches, eyewitnesses, etc., are probably given too much evidentiary value in general. <BR> I also believe that multiple-perp theories -- see Zodiac -- tend to spring swiftly and are fused by disparity in police composite sketches and eyewitness descriptions which don&#39;t coalesce. <BR>One excellent source: &#34;Actual Innocence,&#34; 2000 by Neufeld, Scheck and Dwyer, chapter three, &#39;Seeing Things.&#39; &#40;If you require an arch-conservative source, check out what Mark Fuhrman has said about <BR>eyewitnesses in his book about what he calls the Oklahoma Death Machine, I believe. I don&#39;t recall the title but it&#39;s out there.&#41; <BR> <BR>I have a far-flung thought about Kevin Bright. Before I get into it, one question. I just tried the link <BR>to the KAKE interview in this thread. The interview is still there, but no physical description of BTK by Kevin Bright is in the above story. Was it retracted? Or maybe I read an account elsewhere? <BR> <BR>Kevin Bright. There used to be &#40;still is?&#41; a psychological term, confabulation, wherein the human brain fills in gaps in memory, and what the gaps are filled with is fictional. <BR> <BR>In his case, if confabulation is what occurred, it may have been triggered by guilt over the incident. One who confabulates is not intentionally lying; he is in fact consciously relaying memories which he believes are completely <BR>faithful. <BR><b>IF</b> Kevin Bright struggled with BTK as described, I believe it&#39;s entirely possible that he may have been overwhelmed with guilt, guilt due to a belief that he &#34;somehow could have&#34; &#40;my quotes&#41; saved his sister. &#34;If only I&#39;d done something differently,&#34; &#40;my quotes&#41; would be another example type of guilt. <BR>&#40;It&#39;s a common reaction.&#41; <BR> <BR>By extension, the description of BTK given by Kevin may be a memory which his brain had long since supplied <BR>and thus may be a little inaccurate. This might also account for the mention of the <i>bizarre</i> double misfire of the gun. And, after all, the three BTK composites do not resemble each other, at least not to me.  <BR> <BR>Or, Kevin&#39;s description could be a bullseye. At the time of the Bright attack, was there a <i>written</i> description of the Otero suspect which could be quoted here? I seem to recall both a &#34;Hispanic-appearing male,&#34; and the tall, white male with blond hair. Can someone clear this up, if the information exists in writing? Thanks! <BR> <BR>Finally, I&#39;m not too keen about the thoughts I&#39;ve put forth. I share in the general frustration, and Jenkins&#39; post of 6/11 is particularly indicative of the unease due to the lack of answers to seemingly easy questions. <BR> <BR>Tom, can you say at this point whether or not one of your sources has tagged Bright a definite BTK crime? I tend to believe it&#39;s BTK since the cops fairly quickly stated it was BTK as well. I think the cops said this because BTK sent something which only BTK would know, and the cops sat on the information. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 681-->
<!--Post: 682--><!--Time: 1091427886-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST682"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, August 01, 2004 - 11:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Correction: The bold face &#34;IF&#34; should not be that way in above post, sorry. <BR>I also saw the quote finally, Bright&#39;s description of BTK. Computer problems. <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 682-->
<!--Post: 694--><!--Time: 1091644065-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST694"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Muskogee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Muskogee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, August 04, 2004 - 11:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, good thoughts...I&#39;m in the process of digesting them. <BR> <BR>To add to what you&#39;ve said, here&#39;s the medical definition of confabulation, from my Stedman&#39;s &#40;medical dictionary&#41;:   <BR> <BR>&#34;The making of bizarre and incorrect responses, and a readiness to give a fluent but tangential answer, with no regard whatever to facts, to any question put; seen in amnesia, presbyophrenia, and Wernicke-Korsakoff syndrome.&#34; <BR> <BR>I always think of confabulation in dementia &#40;which  can be caused by a myriad of illnesses, included those mentioned above&#41;.  However, I recall &#40;maybe I&#39;m confabulating!&#41; the term as George is using it from my psych. courses in undergrad.  If I&#39;m recalling correctly, it&#39;s as George stated above. <BR> <BR>As a side-note to descriptions based on race, people&#39;s memory can conform to what they believe they are seeing.  For example, I&#39;ve been described  as White, Hispanic, and Native American &#40;I&#39;m White and Native American&#41;.  Those who describe me as Hispanic or Native American almost always say I have black hair and brown eyes &#40;Correct answer is brown hair and hazel eyes&#41;.  I took a psych. course on sterotyping and prejudice in undergrad and, &#40;again!&#41; from what I recall, this is common.  The memory changes and conforms to fit what the person&#39;s image of that race is.   <BR> <BR>Another example was a friend of mine who&#39;s Puerto Rican.  She has blonde hair and very fair skin.  She would get her makeup done in a department store.  If she mentioned that she&#39;s Puerto Rican, they&#39;d always use a foundation that was too dark and have to redo it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 694-->
<!--Post: 696--><!--Time: 1091676308-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST696"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, August 04, 2004 - 8:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks, Dr. Musk, <BR>As a recovering alkie, I remember a rehab roommate who had Korsakoff&#39;s; very intelligent, but in one area he demonstrated the &#34;psychosis,&#34; as I believe it was then called. &#40;Today everything seems to be a &#34;syndrome,&#34; which is probably a more accurate description.&#41;  <BR> <BR>He was fifty-six, I remember, &#40;I was twenty-one&#41; and he claimed he had been the following: a minor league baseball player, &#34;a captain in the Navy,&#34; <BR>a dealer in rare jewels, and several other things. <BR>If you didn&#39;t know he was in treatment, he was entirely believable. But his condition was  induced by a toxin, ethanol, and was purely organic. <BR> <BR>This is <i>not</i>, of course, the case with Kevin <BR>Bright and &#34;confabulation&#34; may be the wrong term. <BR> <BR>I believe Katherine and Kevin Bright were BTK assaults. I do wonder about the strange double misfiring of the weapon. I also notice that Katherine Bright is listed as having been stabbed and not strangled. I can&#39;t ignore this, but I don&#39;t place as much significance in it as others do -- the sole advantage of being an amateur, I&#39;m expected to be wrong about many things. <BR> <BR>Having shot him twice, BTK must have had Kevin on his mind, perhaps obliterating the serial killer&#39;s preconceived, vivid fantasy of how the Bright attack would play out.  <BR> <BR>I think it likely that BTK stabbed <BR>Katherine to hasten her demise, and that this time, unlike the Otero attack, additional people at the scene weren&#39;t dealt with &#34;successfully.&#34;   <BR> <BR>&#40;That BTK didn&#39;t go back to make sure Kevin had expired is not in keeping with a highly organized killer -- kinda like BTK using cord found in the Otero home, rather than bringing <i>enough</i> material with him -- and indicates a murderer still &#34;progressing&#34;.&#41; All in all, BTK was still closer to organized than disorganized, particulary in planning.  <BR> <BR>The final reason I consider this a BTK crime is that one can find anomalies at several BTK crime scenes. BTK claims, although I&#39;ve never believed him, that the Vian children were saved by a ringing phone. If this is true, <u>it means the phone lines weren&#39;t cut.</u> Yet Vian is a definite BTK crime.  <BR> <BR>One other: That BTK targeted Katherine Bright, a grown woman, indicates to me that Julie Otero and not Josephine may have been the primary target only a few months earlier. Maybe BTK intended to hang Julie, too, but she was too heavy. Who knows? <BR> <BR>In fact, here&#39;s a link to one page of an interview with the premiere authority on the subject of sexual sadism. Read carefully, note the example Hazelwood goes into detail with, then note the questions he, Hazelwood, asks. As you&#39;ll see, only the killer <i>really</i> knows: <BR><a href="http://www.crimelibrary.com/criminal_mind/profiling/hazelwood/5.html?sect=20" target=_top>http://www.crimelibrary.com/criminal_mind/profilin g/hazelwood/5.html?sect=20</a> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 696-->
<!--Post: 697--><!--Time: 1091692366-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST697"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, August 05, 2004 - 12:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I misspelled Kathryn&#39;s first name. Sorry.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 697-->
<!--Post: 698--><!--Time: 1091716917-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST698"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Muskogee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Muskogee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, August 05, 2004 - 7:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, as usual, you bring up some very good points.  I have a deep respect for Mr. Hazelwood&#39;s work, and I appreciate the link &#40;I&#39;ve visited the Crime Library numerous times, yet managed to miss this one!&#41;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 698-->
<!--Post: 699--><!--Time: 1091758337-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST699"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, August 05, 2004 - 7:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I like Hazelwood, as he keeps professional jealousies to a minimum, something his former colleagues don&#39;t always do. At any rate, Kathryn and Kevin Bright are to me definite BTK victims, and that makes Kevin Bright&#39;s BTK description, in his interview, <i>the</i> one to rely upon. But it was thirty years ago...we need more information, such as those letters.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 699-->
<!--Post: 1212--><!--Time: 1097777408-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1212"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nostone<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nostone<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, October 14, 2004 - 11:10 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->As I stated in a post in the Otero thread, I&#39;m not completely certain that Bright is a BTK victim.  I&#39;m kinda 60/40 on this, though.  Several eyewitness reports &#40;before/after Oteros, fireman, postal worker&#41; report him as a white man with blonde or brown hair.  Kevin Bright says the man who attacked them was dark skinned.  I absolutely, positively believe Kevin Bright that the person who attacked him and killed his sister looks exactly like he described him.  Just not sure it&#39;s the same person as BTK.  Also, the voice on the Fox phone call &#34;sounds&#34; like a white guy to me.  I don&#39;t know why, maybe a preconceived notion, but he sounds white.   <BR> <BR>And I also like Roy Hazlewood and agree with George and Muskogee&#39;s comments about him.  He&#39;s a class act.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1212-->
<!--Post: 1213--><!--Time: 1097777790-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1213"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nostone<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nostone<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, October 14, 2004 - 11:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Of course on the flip side, how much of a coincidence would it be to have 2 killers use the same techniques &#40;and weapons to an extent&#41; a few months and blocks apart.  Strangling, gun for control, knife &#40;there was blood reported at the Otero crime scene, maybe he stabbed someone and LE withheld this&#41;, calm and collected, slips out the back door while there is a commotion out front with Kevin getting help. <BR> <BR>This one is definitely up in the air for me, but not by much.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1213-->
<!--Post: 2470--><!--Time: 1103724888-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2470"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 22, 2004 - 6:14 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Last night I found a site in which Kevin is quoted as saying that the killer had on an orange shirt and orange jacket. I wish the facts on these cases were clear. I cannot imagine someone wanting to kill and leave unnoticed and wear orange. Oh, well.......The more confusing the facts, the more cover is provided for BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2470-->
